.TH ASIKA 1 "2026-05-04" "Asika" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asika \- Asika PR Manager CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asika
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [SUBCOMMAND] [ARGUMENTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asika is a multi-platform pull request management tool. The CLI interacts with the asikad daemon to manage PRs across GitHub, GitLab, and Gitea platforms from a single interface.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " token"
.BI \-\-token " token"
JWT token for authentication.
Can also be set via
.B ASIKA_TOKEN
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-s " url"
.BI \-\-server " url"
asikad server address (default: http://localhost:8080).
Can also be set via
.B ASIKA_SERVER
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-o " format"
.BI \-\-output " format"
Output format: table, json, yaml (default: table).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS asika completion
Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
Usage:
.B asika completion
[bash|zsh|fish|powershell]
.SS asika config
Manage asikad configuration.
.TP
.B asika config show
Show current config (secrets masked).
.TP
.B asika config set
[\-\-file " path"]
Set config from file or stdin (TOML format).
.TP
.B asika config reload
Trigger hot reload of config.
.SS asika init
Run configuration wizard (sends setup to server).
.SS asika login
Login to asikad and save token for future requests.
.SS asika pr
Manage pull requests.
.TP
.B asika pr list
[group] [\-\-state open|closed|merged] [\-\-platform github|gitlab|gitea]
[\-\-is_draft true|false] [\-\-author " name"]
[\-\-label " label"] [\-\-created_after " time"]
[\-\-updated_after " time"] [\-\-page " n"] [\-\-per_page " n"]
List PRs with filters.
.TP
.B asika pr show
[group] [id]
Show PR details.
.TP
.B asika pr approve
[group] [id]
Approve PR.
.TP
.B asika pr close
[group] [id]
Close PR.
.TP
.B asika pr reopen
[group] [id]
Reopen PR.
.TP
.B asika pr spam
[group] [id] [\-\-undo]
Mark/unmark as spam.
.TP
.B asika pr comment
[group] [id] [body]
Comment on PR.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-approve
[group] [id1,id2,...]
Batch approve PRs.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-close
[group] [id1,id2,...]
Batch close PRs.
.TP
.B asika pr batch\-label
[group] [id1,id2,...] \-\-label " name" [\-\-color " hex"]
Batch add label to PRs.
.SS asika queue
Manage merge queue.
.TP
.B asika queue list
[group]
Show merge queue.
.TP
.B asika queue recheck
[group]
Trigger queue recheck.
.SS asika rules
Manage label rules (auto-labeling by file patterns).
.SS asika self\-update
Update asika/asikad to the latest version.
.TP
Options:
[\-\-version " tag"] [\-\-check] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-yes] [\-\-rollback] [\-\-restart]
.TP
Examples:
.B asika self\-update \-\-check
.br
.B asika self\-update
.br
.B asika self\-update \-\-rollback
.SS asika stale
Manage stale PRs.
.TP
.B asika stale check
[group] [\-\-dry\-run]
Check for stale PRs.
.TP
.B asika stale unmark
[group] [id]
Remove stale label.
.SS asika sync
Manage sync history (multi mode).
.TP
.B asika sync history
Show sync history.
.TP
.B asika sync retry
[sync_id]
Retry failed sync.
.SS asika user
Manage users (admin only).
.SS asika version
Print version information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASIKA_TOKEN
JWT token for authentication.
.TP
.B ASIKA_SERVER
asikad server address.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/asika/config.json
CLI configuration file storing token and server settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asikad (1)
\- Asika daemon documentation.
.SH AUTHORS
Asika Project.
